ense</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Breast imaging with positron emission tomography and fluorine-18 fluorodeoxyglucose: use and limitations</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2000</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>3495</fpage><lpage>3502</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11032590</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schirrmeister</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>K&#x000fc;hn</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Guhlmann</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Santjohanser</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>H&#x000f6;rster</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>N&#x000fc;ssle</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Fluorine-18 2-deoxy-2-fluoro-D-glucose PET in the preoperative staging of breast cancer: comparison with the standard staging procedures</article-title><source>Eur J Nucl Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>358</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11315604</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Noh</surname><given-names>DY</given-names></name><name><surname>Yun</surname><given-names>IJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>YC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Chung</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Detection of cancer in augmented breast by positron emission tomography</article-title><source>Eur J Surg</source><year>1999</year><volume>165</volume><fpage>847</fpage>